  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome in each lottery, but in this case, neither lottery has one. The individual does not mention certainty, sure outcomes, or any related concept. Instead, their justification is based entirely on the higher prize in Lottery B, despite the lower probability. There is no overlap between the information used by the individual (prize size, disregard for small probability differences) and the information relevant to the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome). Furthermore, the individual’s justification (favoring higher reward) is unrelated to the reason’s rule (favoring absence of a sure outcome). Since the reason cannot clearly apply (both lotteries lack sure outcomes) and the individual’s reasoning is based on a completely different criterion, it is certain that the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
